{
  "$schema": "../../templates/component-starter/manifest.schema.json",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "dotbench.esp32-blink-echo",
  "name": {
    "en": "ESP32: blink and UART echo",
    "pt-BR": "ESP32: pisca e eco UART",
    "es": "ESP32: parpadeo y eco UART"
  },
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "author": {
    "name": "dotbench",
    "url": "https://dotbench.app"
  },
  "license": "GPL-3.0-or-later",
  "description": {
    "en": "An ESP32 running real Arduino code: it blinks the on-board LED and echoes every byte it receives on UART1 (RX is GPIO16, TX is GPIO17, 115200 baud, 8N1) back to the sender. Wire the Kode Dot's UART TX to RX and its RX to TX. The console shows what the sketch prints.",
    "pt-BR": "Um ESP32 rodando código Arduino de verdade: pisca o LED da placa e devolve cada byte recebido na UART1 (RX é o GPIO16, TX é o GPIO17, 115200 baud, 8N1) a quem enviou. Ligue o TX da UART do Kode Dot no RX e o RX no TX. O console mostra o que o sketch imprime.",
    "es": "Un ESP32 con código Arduino real: parpadea el LED de la placa y devuelve cada byte recibido en la UART1 (RX es el GPIO16, TX es el GPIO17, 115200 baudios, 8N1) a quien lo envió. Conecta el TX de la UART del Kode Dot al RX y su RX al TX. La consola muestra lo que imprime el sketch."
  },
  "category": "mcu",
  "tags": [
    "esp32",
    "uart",
    "arduino",
    "blink"
  ],
